<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan money, bond markets closed for holiday.</title>
<headline>Taiwan money, bond markets closed for holiday.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's money and bond markets were closed on Thursday for the National Day holiday. They will reopen on Friday.</p>
<p>On Wednesday, the overnight interbank rate finished at 4.804 percent against Tuesday's close of 4.846 percent, with 30-day commercial paper unchanged at 4.70-4.75.</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
</text>
